{
  "title": "Rescrape update drops the recipe's tags",
  "description": "The rescrape update path (SaveRecipeStep::update_recipe in \
server/src/scraping/steps.rs, now `create_new_version(conn, &new_version, \
TagSource::None)` via the shared write service in server/src/recipes.rs) \
creates the new recipe version with no recipe_version_tags rows. Since the \
recipe's tags live on the current version, rescraping a recipe silently drops \
every tag the user has applied.\n\
\n\
Every other new-version path carries tags forward (normalize-title, \
generate-description, generate-photo, photo-only rescrape, auto-tags), so this \
looks like an oversight rather than a decision. Discovered while extracting \
the shared recipe-version write service; preserved as-is there because fixing \
it is a behavior change.\n\
\n\
Fix: switch the update_recipe call to TagSource::CopyFrom(current version id) \
so tags survive a rescrape, and add an e2e assertion in tests/test_rescrape.py \
(tagged recipe -> rescrape -> tags unchanged). Decide first whether any \
rescrape flow intentionally resets tags. Server-side only; no client changes. \
No `make pipeline` data/ diffs expected (tags are not part of pipeline \
snapshot output).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "pipeline",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-02T13:10:00-07:00",
